==English==

===Etymology===
The phrase, first attested in 1896, refers to the practice of a grocer using a long stick to push a can of goods off a high shelf. (See [https://web.archive.org/web/20101205010211/https://www.seattlepi.com/baseball/33209_aguy30.shtml Seattle Post Intelligencer - Sports Answer Guy article])

